  #line-at(72.024pt, 82.32pt, "elaborate our micromagnetic model beyond a qualitative agreement with existing experimental ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 101.3pt, "results [17,22-24].  To approximate an infinite extent of the film, periodic boundary conditions ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 120.26pt, "are applied in the in-plane dimensions, alone with a gradual increase of the Gilbert damping ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 139.34pt, "in the ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(105.5pt, 139.34pt, "±𝑥")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(119.9pt, 139.34pt, " directions.  The corresponding procedures are described in the Supplementary ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 158.66pt, "material [27].  The boundaries between the regions of increased and uniform damping lie ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 177.74pt, "approximately 2 µm from the edges of the simulation grid along ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(386.35pt, 177.74pt, "𝑥")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(392.59pt, 177.74pt, ".  The system is relaxed to ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 196.94pt, "its static configuration in the bias magnetic field of 12 mT before applying a suitable dynamic ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 215.9pt, "magnetic field to study its linear and nonlinear dynamics.  ")
  #line-at(100.34pt, 240.86pt, "The linear spectrum of the system is shown in Fig. 1 (b).  The spectrum is obtained by ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 259.82pt, "exciting the region of the disk (but not the YIG film) by a weak, spatially asymmetric broadband ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 278.81pt, "field pulse and then summing the Fourier amplitudes calculated cell-wise from the disk’s ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 297.77pt, "magnetization [17,18,22-26].  The lowest frequency resonance at 1.935 GHz lies well within ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 316.85pt, "the dipolar spin-wave continuum in YIG and is also the strongest and well separated from ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 335.81pt, "higher order modes.  It corresponds to the disk’s edge mode, whose frequency is reduced ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 354.77pt, "(compared to the Kittel frequency of a plane film made of the same material) by the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 373.73pt, "demagnetising field due to the magnetic charges formed at the disk edges [17,18].   ")
  #line-at(100.34pt, 398.69pt, "The dynamic dipolar coupling of the spin waves propagating in YIG to the edge mode ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 417.65pt, "(the ‘local’ mode) leads to their resonant scattering.  To obtain its directivity shown in Fig. 1 (c), ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 436.73pt, "a 1.935 GHz frequency plane spin wave is launched in the ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(363.55pt, 436.73pt, "+𝑥")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(377.95pt, 436.73pt, " direction (0°), after which the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 455.95pt, "scattered wave’s Fourier amplitudes are calculated from the YIG film’s magnetisation for ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 474.91pt, "different reciprocal space directions [28].  The directivity reveals that the resonant scattering ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 493.99pt, "is chiral, i.e. the disk acts as a chiral magnonic resonator with minimal backscattering [12].  ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 512.95pt, "The strong forward-backward asymmetry facilitates implementing feed-forward networks of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 531.91pt, "such neurons.  In the reciprocal space, the scattering occurs into a wide angle of about ±60°.  ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 550.87pt, "However, the anisotropic magnonic dispersion of the in-plane magnetised YIG film [29,30]  ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 569.83pt, "means that the scattering angle shrinks by about a half in the real space, i.e. when considered ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 588.79pt, "in terms of the directions of the group velocity.  This scattering angle determines the number ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 607.75pt, "of other neurons with which the given one would be able to communicate (i.e. receive from or ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 626.74pt, "feed to) the signal.   ")
  #line-at(100.34pt, 651.82pt, "Before we present our results of nonlinear spin-wave scattering from the nano-disk, we ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 670.78pt, "first characterise the nonlinearity of its edge mode resonance.  We drive the nano-disk placed ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 689.74pt, "above the YIG film (but not the film itself) by a monochromatic spatially-uniform circularly ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 708.7pt, "polarised magnetic field of the form ")
